       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "9575189"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Reversibly inhibits the activity of ATP2A1/SERCA1 and ATP2A2/SERCA2 in sarcoplasmic reticulum by decreasing the apparent affinity of the ATPase for Ca(2+) (PubMed:11781085, PubMed:9575189). Also inhibits the activity of ATP2A3/SERCA3 (By similarity). Modulates calcium re-uptake during muscle relaxation and plays an important role in calcium homeostasis in muscle. Required for muscle-based, non-shivering thermogenesis (By similarity)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "FUNCTION"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250",
       "source": "UniProtKB",
       "id": "P42532"
      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250",
       "source": "UniProtKB",
       "id": "Q9CQD6"
      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "28890335"
      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "36523160"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Homooligomer (PubMed:36523160). Can also form heterooligomers with other sarcoplasmic/endoplasmic reticulum calcium ATPase (SERCA) regulators ARLN, ERLN, PLN and STRIT1/DWORF (PubMed:36523160). Monomer (By similarity). Interacts with calcium ATPase ATP2A1/SERCA1. Interacts as a monomer with ATP2A2/SERCA2; the interaction decreases ATP2A2 Ca(2+) affinity (PubMed:28890335). Interacts with VMP1; VMP1 competes with PLN and SLN to prevent them from forming an inhibitory complex with ATP2A2 (PubMed:28890335)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "SUBUNIT"
  },
